  "extraction_notes": "[text-pass] The samples are nanocomposites of Sb2Te3 and AgSbTe2. The atomic percentage of Ag is denoted by x. The pristine sample is ST (x=0). AST1, AST2, AST3, and AST4 correspond to x=0.9, 1.70, 5.90, and 7.00 respectively. ZT values for AST3 and AST4 are reported at 375 K. [figure-pass p1-5] The provided pages describe a study of Sb2Te3-AgSbTe2 nanocomposite thin films. While the text mentions ZT values and power factor values, there are no property-vs-temperature plots provided in the images. Therefore, no thermoelectric property data points could be extracted. [figure-pass p6-10] The samples are Ag-doped Sb2Te3 nanocomposites where Ag incorporation leads to the formation of AgSbTe2 secondary phase. Doping site is identified as Sb based on the text. Thermoelectric properties were extracted from Table 1 and Figure 2. [figure-pass p11-14] The provided pages contain theoretical discussions, band structure calculations, and density of states plots (Figure 3) for AgSbTe2/Sb2Te3 heterostructures. However, there are no plots or tables showing thermoelectric properties (Seebeck coefficient, electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity, power factor, or ZT) as a function of temperature for any AgSbTe2-family compounds. ",
